    <property name="text">
     <string>Feedback decoders with a relays extension board can respond to an accessory decoder address in the range between 1..1024. Four relays can be addressed by a single decoder. The decoder stores in its CVs only the first address of such block of four. Examples: 1, 5, 9, ..., 1021. Don't forget to restart the decoder after the Relays address was changed.</string>
